<%# Blacklight's search tips, with the gem's unclosed <li> tags and its mismatched <h2>...</h4> fixed, and the card's heading a real heading in order %>
<section class="advanced-search-tips" aria-labelledby="advanced-search-tips-title">
  <h2 id="advanced-search-tips-title" class="advanced-search-tips__title">Search tips</h2>
  <ul class="advanced-help">
    <li>Select "match all" to require all fields.</li>
    <li>Select "match any" to find at least one field.</li>
    <li>Combine keywords and attributes to find specific items.</li>
    <li>Use quotation marks to search as a phrase.</li>
    <li>Use "+" before a term to make it required. (Otherwise results matching only some of your terms may be included).</li>
    <li>Use "-" before a word or phrase to exclude.</li>
    <li>Use "OR", "AND", and "NOT" to create complex boolean logic. You can use parentheses in your complex expressions.</li>
    <li>Truncation and wildcards are not supported - word-stemming is done automatically.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="advanced-search-tips__subtitle">Match types</h3>
  <ul class="advanced-match-types">
    <li><strong>Contains all</strong> finds records with every word you type in that field.</li>
    <li><strong>Contains any</strong> finds records with at least one of the words.</li>
    <li><strong>Excludes</strong> leaves out records that have the words.</li>
    <li>Under each attribute, <strong>Includes all</strong> needs every ticked value, <strong>Includes any</strong> needs at least one, and <strong>Excludes all</strong> leaves out records with any of them.</li>
    <li>Use <strong>Add a field</strong> to search more fields, and the cross to remove one.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
